# Engineering standard (tier 0)

## MUST (all projects)

- Domain/control flow uses plain classes, explicit dependencies, testable design
- State: one writer per concern; commands via services; notifications via events
- Rule of Three for abstractions; interfaces allowed for DI, tests, or 2+ implementations
- Orchestrators depend on abstractions for time, random, persistence, external IO
- Tests: domain rules get unit tests; Arrange-Act-Assert layout
- Production: no secrets in repo; validate user input; fail fast on wiring errors
- Readability: one type per file; match local style; no dead commented code

## Audit focus

- Constructor injection vs service locator
- Static mutable state in domain logic
- Number of dependencies per class (flag if over 5)
- Separation of concerns between orchestration and data access
